<title>GERMANY: Agiv down after MG decision.</title>
<headline>Agiv down after MG decision.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in German industrial holding company Agiv AG fell one mark, or 3.46 percent, to 28 marks on Friday after Metallgesellschaft AG said it had decided not to buy a 49.99 percent stake in the group.</p>
<p>MG said on Thursday it had decided not to purchase the stake, currently held by BHF Bank, after the due-diligence process was halted following negative press reports.</p>
<p>BHF shares were also down in pre-bourse IBIS trade, falling 0.75 marks to 40.20 marks.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
